    "findings": [
      "NativeEditor readiness follows public Rendered plus documentReady viewport/skeleton/input checks; neither establishes that a global dialog component has rendered.",
      "NativeCopyPlugin.onRendered creates IDialogService, whose constructor registers the global DialogPart or MobileDialogPart. useComponentsOfPart debounces registration by 200 ms.",
      "DesktopDialogService publishes open options through a plain Subject with no replay; MobileDialogService inherits it. Redi useObservable subscribes during the dialog component first render.",
      "The baseline trace records OPEN with zero observers before first GET_DIALOGS and no dialog in both phone cases, establishing the missed emission.",
      "The public Steady lifecycle is documented as feature readiness; the installed SDK emits it three seconds after Rendered. The candidate uses that event, not a custom sleep or a retry.",
      "FUniver inherits public disposeWithMe and disposes with its injector. The candidate removes its listener before its single command invocation, or on editor disposal if Steady is not reached."
    ]
  },
